        historical_note: "A seven-shot repeater with a tubular magazine in the stock, loaded through the buttplate. Chambered in .56-56 Spencer rimfire, it saw extensive use by Union cavalry late in the Civil War. More powerful than the Henry but slower to reload due to the buttstock magazine design.",
