        historical_note: "The standard-issue U.S. Army rifle from 1873 through the 1890s. A single-shot .45-70 breech-loader converted from the muzzle-loading Springfield Model 1863, its hinged breechblock gave it the 'trapdoor' name. Used at the Battle of the Little Bighorn and throughout the Indian Wars.",
        sources: ["Frasca, 1975", "McAulay, 1996"],
