        two_handed: false,
        first_year_available: 1700,
        historical_note: "A lightweight axe used by both Native Americans and European colonists as a tool and weapon. The iron trade tomahawk was a common frontier item, used for everything from woodcutting to combat. Could be thrown with lethal accuracy at short ranges.",
