        historical_note: "A long cavalry spear, typically 8 to 10 feet in length, used by Plains tribes and cavalry forces. The Comanche and Lakota were renowned lancers who could wield a lance with devastating effect from horseback. A well-driven lance strike carried the full force of the horse behind it.",
