        first_year_available: 1862,
        historical_note: "Dr. Richard Gatling's hand-cranked machine gun, patented in 1862. A rotating cluster of barrels fed by a hopper, it could deliver 200 rounds per minute. Though adopted too late for significant Civil War use, it was used in post-war conflicts and was both terrifying and mechanically unreliable in the field. Appears exactly twice in the campaign.",
